{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates strong structural foundations with proper OWL2 modeling patterns (reification, inverse properties, disjointness). However, it suffers from critical EDIFACT semantic gaps: missing ~60% of mandatory D96A INVOIC segments, absent qualifier distinctions that are fundamental to EDIFACT semantics, and insufficient cardinality constraints for EANCOM business rules. The ontology models abstract concepts well but fails to capture the precise segment-level structure required for D96A compliance.",
  "completeness_score": 0.35,
  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "RFFSegment",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "Reference segment (RFF) is MANDATORY in EANCOM INVOIC for document references like order numbers, delivery note numbers, etc. Without RFF, you cannot link invoices to their originating documents - a core business requirement."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "IMDSegment",
      ", "owl_reviewed_length": 25775, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

